# Python hygiene

- Use `from __future__ import annotations`, dataclasses/enums for public structures, and explicit types on public APIs.
- Match existing phase headers: `# ELIAN — … (Phase N)`.
- Never commit secrets, tokens, or raw transcripts when privacy config forbids it.
- Prefer `subprocess` with argument lists; avoid `shell=True` unless unavoidable and sanitized.
- Unit tests: `unittest` + `FakeModelClient` / dry `ToolRegistry`. No real mic, HA writes, or side-effect tools in unit tests.
- Keep changes focused; do not drive-by refactor unrelated modules.
- Deterministic tests: inject clocks/models; do not depend on live Ollama unless the test/smoke explicitly says so.
